{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on E1 question `4a836ee0`: your boundary stands.\n\n1. The boundary is the runtime's own phase. The current act's output\n   is pending from the first point at which a lookup by number in the\n   real judgment can return the working row.\n2. After that point, a reached lookup by a number that names no\n   recorded item answers `unavailable`, and it lacks `entry`.\n3. Before that point, with no earlier output pending, ordinary absence\n   stays. The real judgment gives the same answer there, because the\n   row does not exist yet.\n4. A provisional open subject counts from the same point and not\n   earlier. If the runtime shows the working row to a guard before any\n   effect runs, the output is pending for that guard.\n5. The typed `from: self` position and the marked `device-command`\n   record keep their rulings. A named source resolves by its token,\n   and a recorded number reads its row.\n\nUse the phase that Core observes. Add no alias map and no allocation\nrule.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}